WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:26.921
Both searches return three. Did both search the same way?

00:00:26.921 --> 00:01:00.897
A term pointer and a vector search are different routes

00:01:00.897 --> 00:01:35.958
Examine all six; keep the nearest three

00:01:35.958 --> 00:02:12.497
C was closer, but this run never saw it

00:02:12.497 --> 00:02:46.439
Navigate promising neighbours

00:02:46.439 --> 00:03:22.299
Four decisions behind the same top-k output

00:03:22.299 --> 00:04:03.967
Nearest means best available under the rule
